> - **After-School Programs:**
>   - Many working mothers relied on after-school programs or babysitters, which were seen as a patchwork solution that couldn't substitute for the nurturing and guidance provided by a dedicated parent at home.
> 
> ### Conclusion
> 
> Thus, non-working mothers were often idealized as being able to provide a structured, nurturing environment that working mothers were perceived to lack due to their employment commitments. This dichotomy has largely shifted in contemporary society, recognizing that both working and non-working parents can provide loving and productive environments for their children, albeit through different means.
